      "writtenOn": "2024-04-16T01:02:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "1. Currently we have the flags enabled by leveraging sysprops (crrev.com/c/5399300), and audio is almost inaudible without ASRC.\n\n2. Regarding SoC, Android uses the NTP-adjusted clock while CrOS uses the non-adjusted clock. If we were to use this without modification, there will be 3 time domains and the issue will be between the audio server (non-adjusted) and the BT stack (NTP-adjusted).",
      "parentUuid": "85815e36_22efff6d",
